WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.890
Much groundwater occupies pores between sediment grains and fractures in rock.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.110
Connected openings allow water to move;

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.430
an isolated opening can store water without transmitting it well.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.930
A sedimentary rock can therefore act as both a record of

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.370
deposition and a host for a later fluid history.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.450
Oil and natural gas form in organic-rich sedimentary rocks and can

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.570
migrate upward. Some escape, while some collect where rock geometry and

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:29.310
a seal trap them. Distinguish the source that generates petroleum from

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.190
the reservoir that stores it and the trapping conditions that keep

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.850
it underground. A porous bed alone does not prove an oil

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:36.190
field.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.930
Coal comes from buried plant material.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.470
Suitable limestone supplies material for manufactured cement.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.110
Salt can be mined from old deposits or harvested by evaporating

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:50.490
brine. Migrating groundwater can concentrate uranium in sedimentary rocks.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.210
These resources have different origins even when all occur within a

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.350
sedimentary sequence.

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:59.690
Modern sedimentary processes help interpret ancient deposits.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.790
Layers preserve changing environments, fossils, past climate and evidence of events

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.770
such as landslides, storms and earthquakes.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.610
Reconstruct the event from its deposit and context.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.250
The record supports understanding of past change;

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.450
it does not specify the exact date of a future hazard.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.010
Sand and gravel are widely used construction resources.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.310
Material is excavated, screened into sizes and sometimes crushed.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.830
Selected sizes can become concrete aggregate, tile ingredients or fill beneath

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:32.150
roads and buildings. Aggregate is the granular material;

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.870
manufactured cement binds a concrete mixture.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.410
Natural cement between rock grains is another use of the same

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:38.750
word.
